# Docs and OSS Rules

- README must explain problem, solution, status, quick start, configuration, validation, and docs index.
- Feature claims must match source evidence.
- OSS docs should include license, contributing, security reporting, changelog/release policy, examples, and support boundaries when applicable.
- Documentation must mark partial, docs-only, mock-only, not-found, and unknown features clearly.
- Do not put personal AI workspace artifacts in repository docs.
- Update docs when public behavior, config, commands, API/CLI, or feature status changes.
